    <briefdescription>
<para>Utility class representing a non-constant Xor-operand. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>We classify non-constant Xor-Operands into two categories: C1) The operand is in the form &quot;X &amp; C&quot;, where C is a constant and C != ~0 C2) C2.1) The operand is in the form of &quot;X | C&quot;, where C is a non-zero constant. C2.2) <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_any" kindref="compound">Any</ref> operand E which doesn&apos;t fall into C1 and C2.1, we view this operand as &quot;E | 0&quot; </para>
    </detaileddescription>
